Subject: [PATCH] fix(sidebar): list this Mac's chats from the registry primary
 while the window is on another gateway [daveey]

withPrimaryRecents compared the window's request connection with
primaryGatewayConnectionId(), which names the window's own primary SOCKET.
Switching the window to the hub re-homes that socket, so both named the hub,
no local recents were fetched, and every local row fell out of $sessions.
Pinned local rows survived only through the keep set as frozen copies: their
kanban_* stamps refreshed (refreshRetainedKanban) but turn_live, message_count
and outcome did not. A stale turn_live from an ended turn kept the parked chat
20261026_170127_f07c32 painting "working" instead of its stored grey waiting
outcome (session status audit 2026-10-30 22:25 PDT; renderer row turn_live:true
+ 68 msgs vs backend no lease + 53 msgs; $sessions held 50 hub rows + 2 pinned
local rows, no other local row).

ownRecentsConnection() now resolves "this Mac" as the registry primary (the
window's primary socket only without a registry) and reads a local-kind target
passively, so a remote-only client never spawns a local serve for it.
